{
  "requirement": "A bundled skill MAY put material needed only in specialized situations in files it links to. Each such link MUST say when to read the file. Each bundled skill, recognized by its front matter, is a site:\n\n:::{sites} skills\n```yaml\nlanguage: markdown\npaths: [assets/skills]\nrule:\n  kind: minus_metadata\nmatch:\n  - \"---\\nname: example\\n---\\n\\n# Example\\n\"\nno_match:\n  - \"# Example\\n\"\n```\n:::",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations.** The requirement has two obligations.\n- A bundled skill MAY link to files. A MAY imposes nothing to check.\n- Each such link MUST say when to read the file. Each skill upholds this on its own, so the skill is the site and gets its own site review.\n\nNeither obligation needs separate code-level tests. The existing test `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_say_when_to_read_each_reference_file]` is extra assurance. It pins the \"when to read\" wording for each skill's own `references/` files, and it fails if a skill's reference file has no entry in its table.\n\n**Site query `skills`.**\n- I ran `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.references/skills`. It returned exactly five matches, the `SKILL.md` front matter of `habeas`, `habeas-requirements`, `habeas-evidence`, `habeas-bootstrap-requirements` and `habeas-refactor`.\n- These are the same five names as the `SKILLS` const in `tests/authoring_cli.rs`.\n- A search for `^name: habeas` across the repository found no other skill. The reference files under `assets/skills/*/references` have no front matter, so they are rightly not selected.\n- The query therefore selects every bundled skill and nothing outside the stated scope.\n\n**Query snippets.** The match snippet is a document with `---` front matter. The no_match snippet is the same body without front matter. Together they show the `minus_metadata` condition separating a skill from a plain markdown file. The requirement has no violation queries.\n\n**Cross-skill links.** `habeas-bootstrap-requirements` and `habeas-evidence` also link to `../habeas/references/ci.md`, and the test does not check these links. They are links to files the skill links to, so each skill's own site review covers them. The requirement does not assign them to code, so I do not count the missing check as a test gap.\n\nNo gap found.",
  "references": "5b5a1f7cf171bc78f06adc8576f6e3e3dcb20c5f062af5c778e2b34a76dbfa84",
